nel's "},{"id":"spn-23420","marks":["bold"],"text":"resource"},{"id":"spn-23421","text":" rung — the affine ledger where a token is either "},{"id":"spn-23422","marks":["italic"],"text":"depletable"},{"id":"spn-23423","text":" (linear: consumed once) or "},{"id":"spn-23424","marks":["italic"],"text":"reusable"},{"id":"spn-23425","text":" (affine/\"of-course\": intact after use). "},{"id":"spn-23426","marks":["bold"],"text":"Recommendation:"},{"id":"spn-23427","text":" when V0.2 lands, name this correspondence explicitly and reuse the resource-rung vocabulary ("},{"id":"spn-23428","marks":["code"],"text":"consume"},{"id":"spn-23429","text":", "},{"id":"spn-23430","marks":["code"],"text":"0̲"},{"id":"spn-23431","text":" annihilation on overspend) rather than inventing a parallel one. The kernel's "},{"id":"spn-23432","marks":["code"],"text":"resource.mjs"},{"id":"spn-23433","text":" (laws "},{"id":"spn-23434","marks":["code"],"text":"C1–C8"},{"id":"spn-23435","text":", "},{"id":"spn-23436","marks":["code"],"text":"CB1–CB3"},{"id":"spn-23437","text":") is the reference semantics."}]},{"id":"blk-23007","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-23438","text":"4. An optional \"verify\" gate is just an ordinary phase"}]},{"id":"blk-23008","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23439","text":"A loop that wants the kernel to gate a commit declares a normal "},{"id":"spn-23440","marks":["code"],"text":"route"},{"id":"spn-23441","text":" or "},{"id":"spn-23442","marks":["code"],"text":"act"},{"id":"spn-23443","text":" phase whose body calls "},{"id":"spn-23444","marks":["code"],"text":"bridge.select(...)"},{"id":"spn-23445","text":". PULSE needs "},{"id":"spn-23446","marks":["bold"],"text":"no new phase kind"},{"id":"spn-23447","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-23448","marks":["bold"],"text":"no schema change"},{"id":"spn-23449","text":" — the verdict is a phase "},{"id":"spn-23450","marks":["italic"],"text":"body"},{"id":"spn-23451","text":", and its result is an ordinary "},{"id":"spn-23452","marks":["code"],"text":"OutcomeSignal"},{"id":"spn-23453","text":" (or a "},{"id":"spn-23454","marks":["code"],"text":"DeliberationResult"},{"id":"spn-23455","text":" when κ>0). Keep the 5 canonical phase kinds intact."}]},{"id":"blk-23009","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-23456","text":"What this review deliberately does NOT do"}]},{"id":"blk-23010","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-23012","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23457","text":"It does "},{"id":"spn-23458","marks":["bold"],"text":"not"},{"id":"spn-23459","text":" add an 8th invariant, a verdict phase kind, or any required field — the"}]}],"id":"blk-23011","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-23013","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23460","text":"v0.1 schema is unchanged and remains backward compatible."}]},{"id":"blk-23014","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-23016","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23461","text":"It does "},{"id":"spn-23462","marks":["bold"],"text":"not"},{"id":"spn-23463","text":" claim a rung↔phase-kind bijection (the two are orthogonal axes)."}]}],"id":"blk-23015","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-23018","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23464","text":"Enforcement of the deontic/strategic/reflexive rungs stays in the runtime that "},{"id":"spn-23465","marks":["italic"],"text":"hosts"}]}],"id":"blk-23017","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-23019","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23466","text":"the loop (Delegatic for policy/audit), not in the manifest."}]},{"id":"blk-23020","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-23467","text":"Follow-ups (out of scope here)"}]},{"id":"blk-23021","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-23023","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23468","text":"A "},{"id":"spn-23469","marks":["code"],"text":"pulse-conformance"},{"id":"spn-23470","text":" checker that lifts "},{"id":"spn-23471","marks":["code"],"text":"invariants"},{"id":"spn-23472","text":" → 